iv style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(160px,1fr));gap:8px;margin-top:24px\"><div style=\"padding:16px;border-radius:16px;background:#fff\"><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-label),monospace;font-size:11px;color:#6E6C8A\">REGION</div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-top:4px\">West Africa</div></div><div style=\"padding:16px;border-radius:16px;background:#fff\"><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-label),monospace;font-size:11px;color:#6E6C8A\">MAIN BUSINESS CITY</div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-top:4px\">Accra</div></div><div style=\"padding:16px;border-radius:16px;background:#fff\"><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-label),monospace;font-size:11px;color:#6E6C8A\">DIALLING CODE</div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-top:4px\">+233</div></div><div style=\"padding:16px;border-radius:16px;background:#fff\"><div style=\"font-family:var(--font-label),monospace;font-size:11px;color:#6E6C8A\">CURRENCY</div><div style=\"font-weight:600;margin-top:4px\">GHS</div></div></div></div></div></section><section style=\"max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding-left:clamp(20px,4vw,48px);padding-right:clamp(20px,4vw,48px);padding-top:clamp(64px,8vw,112px);\"><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(100%,340px),1fr));gap:clamp(24px,4vw,56px);align-items:start\"><h2 style=\"font-family:var(--font-heading),sans-serif;font-size:clamp(30px, 1.9vw + 23px, 52px);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-0.04em;font-weight:700;margin:0\">Questions about Ghana.</h2><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);gap:8px;grid-column:span 2;min-width:0\"><details open=\"\" style=\"border-radius:20px;background:#fff\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 24px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;line-height:24px\">How long does it take to send money to Ghana?</h3><span style=\"width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:#F6F4EF;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#3B2ED3;flex:none;font-size:18px\">+</span></summary><p style=\"margin:0;padding:0 24px 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#4C4A66\">Most ElementPay payouts to MTN MoMo in Ghana are sent on local rails as soon as you confirm, with a status for every payment.</p></details><details style=\"border-radius:20px;background:#fff\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 24px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;line-height:24px\">Which payout methods are available in Ghana?</h3><span style=\"width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:#F6F4EF;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#3B2ED3;flex:none;font-size:18px\">+</span></summary><p style=\"margin:0;padding:0 24px 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#4C4A66\">ElementPay pays out in GHS to MTN MoMo, Telecel Cash, AT Money and Bank. Mobile money payouts need the recipient’s phone number in +233 format. Bank payouts need the recipient’s account number and bank.</p></details><details style=\"border-radius:20px;background:#fff\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 24px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;line-height:24px\">Can I send money to Ghana with USDC or USDT?</h3><span style=\"width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:#F6F4EF;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#3B2ED3;flex:none;font-size:18px\">+</span></summary><p style=\"margin:0;padding:0 24px 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#4C4A66\">Yes. Hold USDC or USDT in your ElementPay balance and use it to fund any payout to Ghana. ElementPay converts to GHS at a rate shown before you confirm and delivers on the local rail.</p></details><details style=\"border-radius:20px;background:#fff\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 24px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;line-height:24px\">Can I hold GHS in an ElementPay account?</h3><span style=\"width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:#F6F4EF;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#3B2ED3;flex:none;font-size:18px\">+</span></summary><p style=\"margin:0;padding:0 24px 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#4C4A66\">Yes. ElementPay issues GHS bank accounts, one per currency, so you can receive, hold and pay in Ghanaian cedis.</p></details><details style=\"border-radius:20px;background:#fff\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 24px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;line-height:24px\">What currency does the recipient receive in Ghana?</h3><span style=\"width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:#F6F4EF;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#3B2ED3;flex:none;font-size:18px\">+</span></summary><p style=\"margin:0;padding:0 24px 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#4C4A66\">Recipients in Ghana are paid in Ghanaian cedis (GHS). You can fund the payout from USD, EUR, GBP, any of ElementPay’s 30 account currencies, or USDC and USDT.</p></details><details style=\"border-radius:20px;background:#fff\"><summary style=\"cursor:pointer;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:22px 24px\"><h3 style=\"margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:500;line-height:24px\">Is ElementPay a bank?</h3><span style=\"width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:50%;background:#F6F4EF;display:grid;place-items:center;color:#3B2ED3;flex:none;font-size:18px\">+</span></summary><p style=\"margin:0;padding:0 24px 22px;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#4C4A66\">No. ElementPay is a financial technology company. Banking services are provided by licensed partner institutions.</p></details></div></div></section><section style=\"max-width:1240px;margin:0 auto;padding-left:clamp(20px,4vw,48px